    {
      "section": "Version and snapshot semantics",
      "text": "- **Cross-profile drift** compares actual installed registry artifacts. `link:` working trees and `file:` snapshots stay visible but do not define the registry baseline.\n- **Upstream checks** read your npm registry configuration, keep cache entries isolated by registry and package name, redact credentials from errors, and return `behind`, `current`, `ahead`, `local`, or `unknown`.\n- **Snapshots** live under `~/.config/dsh-harbor/` and track profile membership as well as artifact identity, so profile swaps and upgrades cannot disappear behind deduplication."
    },
    {
      "section": "Trust model and limits",
      "text": "- Harbor is a **read-only mirror**, not a sandbox, installer gate, or policy engine.\n- The default scan never contacts the network. The upstream check is the sole networked panel action.\n- Source, manifest, and freshness reads are bounded, regular-file-only, and no-follow; skipped or over-limit coverage is surfaced.\n- Runtime waterfall dispatch modes are not enumerable in the current host API, so Harbor marks that runtime evidence as unavailable instead of guessing.\n- Static analysis can produce false positives and false negatives. Evidence is for review, not blind enforcement."
    },
